  "edgeRules": [
    "Input is split on LF. A trailing CR is stripped from each line. A line of only ASCII whitespace is ignored.",
    "Each line is parsed on its own as one JSON value. A line that does not parse as a JSON object (not JSON, truncated, an array, a string) contributes nothing to the chain.",
    "Only a top-level string `uuid` joins the chain, in file order. A uuid that is not a string (number, null, array, object) is ignored. Duplicate uuid values in the file stay in the chain, in order.",
    "A line that repeats a key (`uuid` or `sessionId` twice in the same object) is skipped as a whole, like serde's duplicate-field error. Mirrors must reject such a line too.",
    "Only `uuid` and `sessionId` are interpreted. Every other field and unknown line shape is ignored.",
    "Chains are compared as exact string sequences: equal means AlreadyCurrent, a strict prefix of the incoming chain means Replace, anything else means Diverged.",
    "Only top-level KEY strings and the values of `uuid` and `sessionId` are checked beyond JSON syntax (escapes, paired surrogates, valid UTF-8, finite numbers, nesting depth 127). A lone surrogate escape, invalid UTF-8 bytes, an out-of-range number such as 1e400 or deep nesting inside any other field does NOT drop the line. A line that is a JSON array of exactly two values is read positionally like serde reads a struct (the first value is `uuid`, the second `sessionId`); any other array contributes nothing."
  ]
